WEBVTT

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:04.520
No way!

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:17.250
Hey, Shiraishi Yoshitake.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:19.460
We meet again.

00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:23.960
Sugimoto Saichi!

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:28.430
I guess you really are immortal!

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:30.510
Where's Asirpa-san?

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:33.600
She's with me.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.630
She's just up ahead...

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:38.840
With Kiroranke and Ogata.

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:43.660
Ogata said he saw you dead up-close.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:46.040
He told Asirpa-chan.

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:48.920
He's the bastard who shot me.

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:51.800
Along with her father, 
who was right next to me.

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:54.030
He and Kiroranke.

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:57.030
You're kidding...

00:00:57.910 --> 00:00:59.990
We're getting her back.

00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:02.120
Wait, is that Ryu?

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:11.300
<i>How did I forget something so important?</i>

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:15.430
<i>Aca was so insistent I not forget it.</i>

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:21.520
<i>If it had something to do with wolves, 
I should've remembered when I was with Retar.</i>

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:30.280
<i>That's right... right after he told me 
that name, Aca left. And Retar left, too.</i>

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:38.640
<i>I was trying my best not to think about it,
 so I pushed it out of my mind.</i>

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:07.790
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:18.990
<b>Episode Thirty-Five
Sin and Impurity</b>

00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:24.390
Something wrong, Ogata?

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:27.290
No, it's nothing.

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:30.390
We need to hurry. The wind's picking up.

00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:34.100
Yeah. Let's make shelter over there.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:38.700
Build up ice to block the wind.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:39.920
There's driftwood.

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:41.610
Let's burn it to make a fire.

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:45.580
Asirpa, let's go look for more firewood.

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:46.410
Okay.

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:57.320
Ogata, there's some here.

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:08.560
Asirpa, you just remembered 
something very important.

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:13.260
Was it the key to help you 
solve the tattoo code?

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:19.190
You won't tell it to me?

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:23.530
I just want a reward for all the 
fighting and risking my life I've done.

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:27.020
Just like Shiraishi and Sugimoto.

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:31.310
I don't need enough money to make a country.

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:34.900
If I tried to take it all, instead of being 
able to live a life of luxury by myself,

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:38.790
I might just find myself 
at the center of a new war.

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:44.800
If you tell me how to break the code, 
you can be free of these killings.

00:04:46.130 --> 00:04:49.820
You can just go back to your kotan 
and let your grandma see that you're safe.

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:54.680
Spend the rest of your life in freedom, 
hunting deer in the nearby mountains.

00:04:56.090 --> 00:04:57.980
That's what you want, right, Asirpa?

00:05:00.470 --> 00:05:02.440
Sugimoto's footsteps are here.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:07.240
Somebody's out here!

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:15.940
Hey, wait!

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:21.800
<i>I don't have time to waste on her.</i>

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:30.370
You Svetlana?

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:33.290
You know me?

00:05:33.990 --> 00:05:37.980
Your parents at the lighthouse saved my life.

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:45.380
They said you were kidnapped by a Russian 
soldier and asked me to save you.

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:49.250
What are you doing here? Are you alone?

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:57.520
I was willing to follow 
anyone who'd take me away.

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:03.300
I wanted to escape from my boring, 
empty life on that island...

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:08.800
Stand.

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:13.700
There's a dog sled over there. 
Go there and wait. You're going home.

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:18.210
I want to see the city! St. Petersburg!

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:24.500
At least let them know you're alive!

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:28.880
Do you know how they feel waiting for you?

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:31.410
How can you be so cruel?

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:36.060
I can't tell them I and that man 
became robbers and got caught...

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:40.890
I didn't want them to know.

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:03.020
Leave your clothes and your things!

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:12.840
Just let Kiroranke and 
Sofia handle the Ainu.

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:16.540
There's no need for you to bear that burden.

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:18.540
Tell me, Asirpa.

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:26.800
Then why are you asking me when 
Kiroranke Nispa isn't around?

00:07:30.070 --> 00:07:31.300
Asirpa!

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:33.990
How far did they go?

00:07:33.990 --> 00:07:36.310
Asirpa! Ogata!

00:07:41.250 --> 00:07:42.950
<i>The same gun shot as before!</i>

00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:53.800
<i>Immortal Sugimoto!</i>

00:07:56.760 --> 00:07:58.300
<i>I knew he was still alive!</i>

00:07:58.300 --> 00:07:59.180
Pursuers?

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:04.170
<i>I can't see anything with 
all this snow and ice.</i>

00:08:04.430 --> 00:08:07.700
Hurry! This is our only 
chance to get close to him,

00:08:07.700 --> 00:08:09.460
while there's still this wind and snow!

00:08:12.310 --> 00:08:14.150
Be careful, Sugimoto!

00:08:14.150 --> 00:08:16.930
The sea currents make the ice floes unstable!

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:19.690
We're being swept away!

00:08:19.690 --> 00:08:21.270
What do we do?

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:24.130
Shiraishi, strip naked, jump in
 the water, and push it back!

00:08:24.130 --> 00:08:25.940
Shut up! You do it!

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:31.710
I'll go check out that gunshot. 
You stay here and wait for the others.

00:08:32.310 --> 00:08:33.840
Asirpa!

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:37.010
The others are getting worried.

00:08:37.510 --> 00:08:38.470
We need to go back.

00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:44.070
When Sugimoto and Nopperabo 
were shot at Abashiri,

00:08:44.070 --> 00:08:46.630
Kiroranke was giving someone a signal.

00:08:48.310 --> 00:08:49.620
Come with me, Asirpa.

00:09:03.010 --> 00:09:04.310
Private Tanigaki!

00:09:04.630 --> 00:09:06.100
I'm done here.

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:07.060
What about Tsukishima?

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:11.320
Where are you, Tsukishima! Tsukishima!

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:12.670
Hurry!

00:09:13.980 --> 00:09:17.430
Kiroranke Nispa was signaling someone?

00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:18.310
Why?

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:20.660
For what purpose?

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:25.660
He waited for you to confirm 
that Nopperabo was your father,

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:27.520
and then had someone shoot him.

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:32.150
I don't know what happened 
between him and Wilk,

00:09:32.150 --> 00:09:34.920
but I assume they were 
fighting over the gold.

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:42.430
Why didn't you tell me until now?

00:09:42.430 --> 00:09:46.760
Because you just remembered 
the way to break the code.

00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:50.520
I decided I needed Kiroranke's help for that,

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:52.940
so I said nothing and just watched.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:57.080
I don't care what happens 
as long as I get that gold,

00:09:57.080 --> 00:10:00.280
but it's dangerous to stay 
with Kiroranke any longer.

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:03.580
He may kill you after he gets the code.

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:06.700
Me and Shiraishi, too.

00:10:07.530 --> 00:10:09.040
Kiroranke Nispa...

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:11.120
Tsukishima!

00:10:12.890 --> 00:10:14.240
Who's that woman?

00:10:14.700 --> 00:10:16.800
The daughter of the couple at the lighthouse.

00:10:17.310 --> 00:10:18.580
What are you talking about?

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:20.220
Leave her!

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:46.110
Tell me, Asirpa, please!

00:10:46.110 --> 00:10:47.790
What did you remember?

00:10:52.110 --> 00:10:53.920
<i>I need to learn it fast.</i>

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:56.380
<i>Or he'll catch up to me.</i>

00:11:23.610 --> 00:11:26.120
You forgot that at Abashiri Prison.

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:29.910
I came to give it back.

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:34.920
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:11:37.280 --> 00:11:38.510
I'm so cold!

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:42.120
Hoparata!

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:44.930
Go!

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:48.930
Asirpa-san's teachings saved me again!

00:11:57.750 --> 00:11:59.650
Tell me, Asirpa, please!

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:07.410
Sugimoto asked me for help.

00:12:08.510 --> 00:12:09.660
Sugimoto!

00:12:14.090 --> 00:12:17.980
When I got close to the two of them 
after they were shot at Abashiri,

00:12:17.980 --> 00:12:20.550
he was still awake.

00:12:22.570 --> 00:12:23.660
Sugimoto...

00:12:24.210 --> 00:12:26.000
My best friend...

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:31.770
died at Port Arthur.

00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:38.500
Give his wife the gold...

00:12:39.890 --> 00:12:42.370
Just a little bit of it.

00:12:46.150 --> 00:12:51.180
I want to get surgery for her eyes.

00:12:53.220 --> 00:12:54.270
Please...

00:12:56.230 --> 00:12:57.100
Ogata.

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:03.470
You never said a word about that!

00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:05.840
You said he was dead when you saw him!

00:13:06.250 --> 00:13:12.180
Because the last words he spoke 
were about a widow in his homeland.

00:13:12.870 --> 00:13:16.190
Is that what you wanted to hear?

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:20.890
I could never be his friend,

00:13:20.890 --> 00:13:23.690
but he saved my life on this journey.

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:27.280
For the sake of his last request, tell me.

00:13:27.580 --> 00:13:29.500
Did you get her name?

00:13:32.130 --> 00:13:32.910
Yeah.

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:33.750
I think it was...

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:38.040
Tome... give it to Tome.

00:13:38.980 --> 00:13:41.230
That's what I heard.

00:13:41.230 --> 00:13:45.010
But if we ask the army,
we can learn where he grew up.

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:46.420
She won't be hard to find.

00:13:48.290 --> 00:13:49.260
Anything else?

00:13:50.210 --> 00:13:51.680
What did he say?

00:13:52.360 --> 00:13:53.730
I want to

00:13:55.530 --> 00:13:56.560
go home...

00:13:57.580 --> 00:13:59.830
That's what he said.

00:14:00.290 --> 00:14:01.940
So for his sake...

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:03.030
Anything else?

00:14:03.450 --> 00:14:04.880
Tell me everything!

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:07.770
Did he say he wanted to eat something,

00:14:09.290 --> 00:14:10.370
or anything similar before he died?

00:14:13.130 --> 00:14:16.790
Yeah... yeah he did.

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:21.290
I want to eat monkfish stew.

00:14:24.410 --> 00:14:25.640
Monkfish stew?

00:14:29.650 --> 00:14:31.300
That's not Sugimoto.

00:14:32.630 --> 00:14:36.310
Ogata, who are you talking about?

00:14:38.740 --> 00:14:43.230
The Sugimoto I know would've 
said "dried persimmons."

00:14:46.140 --> 00:14:47.080
Let me go!

00:14:49.750 --> 00:14:50.740
Let me go!

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:55.740
Calm down, Asirpa!

00:14:57.450 --> 00:14:58.710
Stay away!

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:01.210
I can't trust a word you say!

00:15:03.470 --> 00:15:07.480
I guess I'm out of time.

00:15:11.810 --> 00:15:15.760
I guess I should've known 
I wouldn't be able to do it myself.

00:15:19.750 --> 00:15:25.270
By the way, I've been wondering one thing...

00:15:25.600 --> 00:15:30.030
I remember when we met.

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:34.280
When Sugimoto tried to 
kill me, you stopped me.

00:15:35.030 --> 00:15:36.200
Sugimoto!

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:47.520
You made a vow to never kill anybody, even 
in the midst of the battle for the gold.

00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:49.300
That always seemed strange.

00:15:50.290 --> 00:15:55.150
Did that father of yours 
never teach you to kill me?

00:15:56.790 --> 00:16:01.080
Do the Ainu idols even require "purity"?

00:16:02.410 --> 00:16:03.680
What are you talking about?

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:07.640
Do it. Kill me.

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:11.650
Nobody in this world is pure.

00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:16.620
As long as you've got a reason inside 
you to kill, you won't even feel guilt.

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:23.250
You want me to give you that reason?

00:16:25.450 --> 00:16:28.500
I'm the one who killed your father.

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:34.080
Do it.

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:36.910
You can do it, too.

00:16:36.910 --> 00:16:39.760
I know you're the same as me.

00:16:59.910 --> 00:17:01.910
I won't kill.

00:17:04.110 --> 00:17:08.460
People like you shouldn't exist.

00:17:12.690 --> 00:17:14.510
Ogata!

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:40.620
I won't let you die like this!

00:17:41.180 --> 00:17:43.120
I won't let you make her a murderer!

00:17:43.720 --> 00:17:47.120
I won't let her have the 
slightest part in your death!

00:17:54.770 --> 00:17:56.170
Asirpa-san!

00:17:58.000 --> 00:17:59.340
Take my hand!

00:18:00.410 --> 00:18:01.300
Sugi...

00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:05.480
Sugimoto!

00:18:19.060 --> 00:18:20.700
I knew you were alive.

00:18:22.800 --> 00:18:26.000
I told you. I'm immortal.

00:18:29.770 --> 00:18:32.780
Come on, you don't want to interrupt.

00:18:35.320 --> 00:18:36.580
You're doing well, I see.

00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:39.150
Have you put on weight?

00:18:43.180 --> 00:18:44.090
Can you stand?

00:18:45.370 --> 00:18:46.810
Let's go.

00:18:47.190 --> 00:18:48.310
I can't let go.

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:51.410
Yeah.

00:18:52.470 --> 00:18:54.430
But we need to follow Kiroranke.

00:18:55.130 --> 00:18:56.010
My...

00:18:57.940 --> 00:19:00.160
My eyelid got stuck and now I can't let go!

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:01.650
Oh, no!

00:19:01.650 --> 00:19:03.350
You got stuck to my metal button...

00:19:03.350 --> 00:19:07.050
Don't move! If you rip it off, 
it'll destroy your eyelid!

00:19:07.050 --> 00:19:07.870
Shiraishi!

00:19:08.690 --> 00:19:09.620
Come here!

00:19:09.870 --> 00:19:11.370
Something wrong?

00:19:11.370 --> 00:19:12.900
Piss on her face!

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:15.430
Do what on my face?

00:19:16.320 --> 00:19:17.380
Wait!

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:19.880
Can you piss, Shiraishi?

00:19:20.900 --> 00:19:24.850
Yeah, my bladder is filled to bursting!

00:19:25.460 --> 00:19:26.590
Stop it!

00:19:26.590 --> 00:19:27.690
Hey!

00:19:27.690 --> 00:19:29.850
Stop it!

00:19:56.940 --> 00:20:00.310
That's enough, Shiraishi.

00:20:00.310 --> 00:20:02.070
I'm okay now.

00:20:02.070 --> 00:20:05.460
Hey, Sugimoto, are you crying?

00:20:06.550 --> 00:20:08.090
That's just your piss.

00:20:08.720 --> 00:20:13.190
<b>Several Minutes Earlier</b>

00:20:13.190 --> 00:20:14.730
Private Tanigaki!

00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:16.380
Who did this to you?

00:20:18.620 --> 00:20:21.510
Kiro...ranke!

00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:24.950
That bastard...

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:25.980
Stay put.

00:20:26.670 --> 00:20:28.050
We'll take care of him.

00:20:29.490 --> 00:20:30.210
Blood...

00:20:30.980 --> 00:20:33.870
He's hurt bad.

00:20:34.530 --> 00:20:36.130
Let's go, Tsukishima!

00:20:36.650 --> 00:20:37.860
Stay there!

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:50.970
This gun is Tanigaki's, right?

00:20:51.570 --> 00:20:53.730
The blood leads over there.

00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:57.310
What's this string?

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:05.720
What was that sound?

00:21:05.720 --> 00:21:06.990
I need to piss!

00:21:08.280 --> 00:21:10.010
A bomb?

00:21:10.010 --> 00:21:10.980
Tsukishima!

00:21:13.370 --> 00:21:16.370
Lt. Koito, are you hurt?

00:21:19.030 --> 00:21:20.500
Don't go alone!

00:21:21.210 --> 00:21:22.760
Damn you!

00:21:28.280 --> 00:21:31.010
No footsteps. Did he fall into the ocean?

00:21:57.990 --> 00:22:00.130
How dare you...

00:22:00.130 --> 00:22:04.270
How dare you hurt my men?!

00:23:35.050 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Next Time
To Live</b>

00:23:36.090 --> 00:23:39.490
Next Time: "To Live"!
